{"Title":"An Act relative to allowing redivision of merger lots in municipalities adopting NetZero code","BillNumber":"H3895","DocketNumber":"HD3458","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"CRF1","Name":"Christopher Richard Flanagan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CRF1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T12:49:44.58"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"CRF1","Name":"Christopher Richard Flanagan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CRF1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T12:49:44.58"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3895/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Flanagan of Dennis, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3895) of Christopher Richard Flanagan relative to authorizing redivision of merger lots in municipalities adopting NetZero code.  Municipalities and Regional Government.","DocumentText":"\tSection 6 of chapter 40A of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following paragraph:-\r\n\tAdjacent lots under common ownership in a municipality that has accepted the provisions of the municipal opt-in specialized stretch energy code developed and promulgated pursuant to clause (14) of section 6 of chapter 25A shall not be merged and treated as a single lot, for local zoning purposes, to bring the lots into compliance with lot area zoning requirements of the municipality.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J10","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J10"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}